<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The Breach Jump's landing damage. A clone of Core's Bomb (Damages_Misc.xml)
    with the building factors turned into the point of the set. DamageWorker.Apply
    multiplies building damage by buildingDamageFactor and then by the passable or
    impassable factor (Bomb is 1 / 2 / 4, and Core's Wall def adds its own x2 for
    Bomb, so a grenade's 50 does 400 to a wall cell and 100 to a door or turret).

    Tuning (2026-09-17, retuned from 30 damage at x20 / 1 / 1 after the pawn damage
    proved too lethal): defaultDamage 20 with x30 / 0.25 / 1 gives 600 to a wall
    cell, the old figure (steel 300, hull 420, granite 510; plasteel 840 and uranium
    750 need the shoulders), and 150 to passable buildings, the same 4:1 wall to
    contents ratio vanilla's Bomb keeps, so a landing takes the door and light
    turrets but leaves an 800 HP grav engine or a 500 HP thruster standing. The
    worker is ours: DamageWorker_Breach scales building damage by the instigator's
    SCWC_BreachPower before these factors, so the shoulders' bonus never reaches
    pawns. Pawn damage 20 (Aerial's jump is 15, a grenade 50). minDamageToFragment
    15 copies Bomb's: without it the whole hit lands as one wound on one random
    part, organs included, and 30 to a heart or brain killed outright; with it a
    hit splits into 2 to 4 wounds of 5 to 10. defaultArmorPenetration 0.15 mirrors
    the value the ability passes; GenExplosion ignores this field whenever it is
    handed a damage amount and would otherwise use damage x 0.015. Blunt armor
    category rather than Bomb's Sharp: it is an impact, and end-game blunt ratings
    run lower than sharp, so the pawn damage lands. Heat energy per cell dropped
    (kinetic, not incendiary); the visual and sound reuse Bomb's, plus our
    SCWC_BreachLanding shockwave ring at the centre (explosionCenterEffecter, fired
    by DamageWorker.ExplosionStart on every breach explosion, so the landing ring
    needs no C# and follows the blast onto planet and space maps alike).
  -->
  <DamageDef>
    <defName>SCWC_Breach</defName>
    <label>breach</label>
    <workerClass>ShipcrackerWarcasket.DamageWorker_Breach</workerClass>
    <externalViolence>true</externalViolence>
    <isExplosive>true</isExplosive>
    <deathMessage>{0} has been crushed by a breaching impact.</deathMessage>
    <hediff>Crush</hediff>
    <hediffSkin>Bruise</hediffSkin>
    <hediffSolid>Crack</hediffSolid>
    <harmAllLayersUntilOutside>true</harmAllLayersUntilOutside>
    <impactSoundType>Blunt</impactSoundType>
    <armorCategory>Blunt</armorCategory>
    <minDamageToFragment>15</minDamageToFragment>
    <defaultDamage>20</defaultDamage>
    <defaultStoppingPower>0.5</defaultStoppingPower>
    <defaultArmorPenetration>0.15</defaultArmorPenetration>
    <buildingDamageFactor>30</buildingDamageFactor>
    <buildingDamageFactorPassable>0.25</buildingDamageFactorPassable>
    <buildingDamageFactorImpassable>1</buildingDamageFactorImpassable>
    <plantDamageFactor>4</plantDamageFactor>
    <corpseDamageFactor>0.5</corpseDamageFactor>
    <explosionAffectOutsidePartsOnly>false</explosionAffectOutsidePartsOnly>
    <explosionCellFleck>BlastDry</explosionCellFleck>
    <explosionCenterEffecter>SCWC_BreachLanding</explosionCenterEffecter>
    <explosionColorCenter>(0.85, 0.85, 0.95)</explosionColorCenter>
    <explosionColorEdge>(0.55, 0.55, 0.65)</explosionColorEdge>
    <soundExplosion>Explosion_Bomb</soundExplosion>
    <combatLogRules>Damage_Bomb</combatLogRules>
  </DamageDef>
</Defs>
